# Docker uploads this whole directory to the daemon before a build starts, and
# re-hashes it on every rebuild. Unfiltered that is ~722 MB here, of which
# ~672 MB is a virtualenv that is useless inside a Linux image (wrong platform,
# and the image installs its own dependencies) and ~49 MB is songs and charts
# that are bind-mounted at runtime anyway. On Docker Desktop that transfer
# crosses a VM boundary, so it dominates the build time before a single
# instruction runs.
#
# Allowlist, not denylist: deny everything, then re-admit what the image needs.
# A denylist fails open — the next virtualenv, cache directory or credential
# file silently rejoins the context and nobody notices until the build is slow
# again or something leaks.
*

!*.py
!requirements.txt
!templates

# Re-denied explicitly, after the allows, because these are the ones where a
# mistake is expensive rather than merely slow. `COPY . .` was baking a live
# YouTube Music Premium session and the Soulseek password into an image layer;
# deleting them in a later step would not help, because layers are immutable
# and anyone with the image can read them straight back out.
.env
.env.*
cookies.txt
.spotimine

# Never useful in the image, and listed so the intent survives an edit to the
# allowlist above.
venv
.venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
songs
static
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
